{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"Fusing the prefix scan into the output kernel removes another launch and reduces the 64-chunk latency to ~0.086 ms. I also found that storing the grouped Gram matrix in FP16 halves its traffic while retaining 99.999% local tolerance compliance (the requirement is 99%); that brings it to ~0.078 ms. I’m checking whether a single FP16 tensor contraction can replace the two-term BF16 compensation without giving up that margin."}}
